from pathlib import Path
import json,hashlib,datetime
W=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
load=lambda p:json.loads((W/p).read_text())
checks={'partition':load('reports/blade_partition.json')['passed'],'partition_membership':load('reports/partition_membership.json')['passed'],'independent_RK4':load('reports/rk4_controls.json')['passed'],'time_refinement':load('reports/rk4_time.json')['passed'],'fine_alternate_integrator':load('reports/rk4_fine_verlet.json')['passed'],'contact_sampling_refinement':load('reports/rk4_space.json')['passed']}
for name in ['edge','broad','slide','miss']:
 r=load('runs/rk4_r4_'+name+'_d1_tol0.002/result.json');checks[name+'_cycle']=all(r['checks'].values())
assert all(checks.values()),checks
protected=load('manifest.json')['protected'];changed=[p for p,h in protected.items() if not Path(p).is_file() or hashlib.sha256(Path(p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()!=h];assert not changed,changed
pres={'checked':len(protected),'changed':changed,'all_unchanged':not changed};(W/'preservation.json').write_text(json.dumps(pres,indent=2))
r={'status':'contact_component_checks_pass_continuing_cut_surface_integration','updated_utc':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(),'checks':checks,'selected':{'module':'src/rk4_contact_gpu.py','timestep_s':12.5e-6,'quadrature_subdivision':4,'kinematics':'affine material maps','geometry':'exact original CAD; validated interior partition solely for integration','contact_law':'unchanged K=1e9 N/m3, mu=.2, vs=.001m/s'},'time_force_relative':load('reports/rk4_time.json')['metrics']['force_relative_max'],'space_force_relative':load('reports/rk4_space.json')['metrics']['force_relative_max'],'alternate_integrator_force_relative':load('reports/rk4_fine_verlet.json')['metrics']['force_relative_max'],'scope':'6 mm intact supported cube, 48 tetrahedra; no physical cut, no tomato, no complete RL environment.','rejected_larger_timesteps_s':[25e-6,50e-6],'physical_laws_changed':False,'numerical_integration_changed':True,'physics_limits_changed':False,'physical_cut':False,'rl_ready':False,'current_setup_changed':False,'preservation':pres,'prior_evidence_correction':'v23 float nearest CAD face routine is unreliable on thin blade triangles; its reported successful contact/clearance fixtures do not qualify other points. Original evidence preserved. v24 queries verify candidates using original double precision triangles.','performance':{'small_cycle_wall_s':load('runs/rk4_r4_edge_d1_tol0.002/result.json')['wall_s'],'simulated_s':.013,'note':'Includes checks, host observations and logging; not an RL throughput result. Spatial/time changes prevent treating all historical timings as like-for-like.'}}
(W/'qualification.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2));(W/'status.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2))
(W/'REPORT.txt').write_text('V24 CONTACT COMPONENT — VERIFIED, CONTINUING IN V25\n\nThe selected exact-domain parallel contact integration and RK4 update pass temporal, spatial, alternate-integrator and independent CPU comparisons for the intact supported coupon. Maximum force difference: 0.111% on timestep halving; 0.538% on quadrature refinement; 0.839% against a much finer alternate integrator. Edge, broad-side, sliding and near-miss cycles complete. Force/penetration stops and transactional rollback pass.\n\nAn important prior defect was found: float nearest-face CAD lookup could select the wrong thin blade triangle. Its distance error reached 26.3 micrometres on the independent audit. Candidate verification against original double-precision triangles reduced maximum distance error to 1.2e-17m on those 10,000 points. The same correction is used by the volume guard. Historical claims are limited accordingly, not silently overwritten.\n\nThe CAD integration partition has exactly the original 74 vertices and every exterior triangle, positive cell volumes, matching total volume, and independent membership/ownership checks. It does not substitute a convex hull.\n\nThe 25 and 50 microsecond RK4 trials fail response comparisons and are rejected. Adaptive per-pair variants hit refinement limits and are retained only as evidence. The selected timestep remains 12.5 microseconds; normal force, friction, bulk constants and all physical limits are unchanged.\n\nThis is not a completed tomato or an RL speed pass. A 13ms, 6mm cube cycle takes about 1.9s including checking/output. New cut faces, paid fracture, support/recontact, complete-loop throughput and a visible tomato remain to be qualified in the continuation.\n\nAll '+str(len(protected))+' protected files match their hashes. Existing Isaac/DiSECt setup is unchanged.\n')
files={str(p.relative_to(W)):hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in W.rglob('*') if p.is_file() and 'cache' not in p.parts and '__pycache__' not in p.parts and p.name!='artifact_hashes.json'};(W/'artifact_hashes.json').write_text(json.dumps(files,indent=2));print(json.dumps({'checks':checks,'protected_files':len(protected),'artifacts':len(files)}))
